WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.433 --> 00:00:01.101 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Thank you.

00:00:01.101 --> 00:00:04.437 align:start size:94% position:6%
People in New York will
tell you stuff about yourself

00:00:04.437 --> 00:00:06.873 size:78% position:39% line:92%
you didn't even know.

00:00:06.873 --> 00:00:09.843 size:78% position:39%
Like I just found out
I have a lost face.

00:00:09.843 --> 00:00:14.714
Whenever I walk in stores,
people are like, "Are you lost?"

00:00:14.714 --> 00:00:16.316 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:16.316 --> 00:00:17.951 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
"Can I help you?"

00:00:17.951 --> 00:00:19.719 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like,
maybe I've been here before.

00:00:19.719 --> 00:00:21.554 line:92%
Maybe I can find my aisle.

00:00:21.554 --> 00:00:23.156 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Give me a chance.

00:00:23.156 --> 00:00:24.557 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:24.557 --> 00:00:26.793 line:92%
Maybe I know how to read.

00:00:26.793 --> 00:00:29.629 align:start size:94% position:6%
I go to clubs,
bouncers always do too much.

00:00:29.629 --> 00:00:32.799
They always like, "You know
I got to check your I.D."

00:00:32.799 --> 00:00:36.403 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:36.403 --> 00:00:38.972 align:start size:94% position:6%
You don't have to do all that.
I'm born in the '80s.

00:00:38.972 --> 00:00:42.042 size:78% position:39%
Once you see that 8,
give me my I.D. back.

00:00:42.042 --> 00:00:45.779
I don't care if it's birth date,
issue date, death date,

00:00:45.779 --> 00:00:47.714 size:88% position:44% line:92%
I'm supposed to be here.

00:00:47.714 --> 00:00:49.916 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I'm TSA pre-check.

00:00:49.916 --> 00:00:52.352 align:start size:94% position:6%
I shouldn't have to
go through this.

00:00:52.352 --> 00:00:54.154 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:54.154 --> 00:00:57.891 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:00.527 --> 00:01:02.362 line:92%
I didn't always do comedy.

00:01:02.362 --> 00:01:06.699 align:start size:94% position:6%
I used to work at
a chicken restaurant...

00:01:06.699 --> 00:01:09.135 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
at the airport.

00:01:09.135 --> 00:01:11.538 align:start size:94% position:6%
A lot of people complain
about their commute to work,

00:01:11.538 --> 00:01:14.908 size:81% position:41%
but those people don't
have to go through TSA

00:01:14.908 --> 00:01:17.444 size:75% position:38% line:92%
to get to a kitchen.

00:01:17.444 --> 00:01:19.879 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:19.879 --> 00:01:21.448 line:92%
I don't know if you ever looked

00:01:21.448 --> 00:01:23.149 align:start size:94% position:6%
in the back of
a fast food restaurant,

00:01:23.149 --> 00:01:24.784 align:start size:94% position:6%
but there are no chairs
back there.

00:01:24.784 --> 00:01:27.320 align:start size:94% position:6%
My friends used to complain
about their jobs,

00:01:27.320 --> 00:01:31.191
and they used to be like, "Man,
I just want to do what I love,"

00:01:31.191 --> 00:01:34.894 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I used to be like,
"I just want to sit down."

00:01:34.894 --> 00:01:37.897 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:37.897 --> 00:01:42.235 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:44.404 --> 00:01:45.605 line:92%
I had an interview after that.

00:01:45.605 --> 00:01:47.173 align:start size:94% position:6%
They were like,
"Sir, have a seat."

00:01:47.173 --> 00:01:49.175 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was like,
"I'm so happy to be here."

00:01:49.175 --> 00:01:52.312 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
"Thank you so much."

00:01:52.312 --> 00:01:55.648 align:start size:94% position:6%
Working there,
they would only hire people

00:01:55.648 --> 00:01:58.685 align:start size:94% position:6%
to work the cash register
who were bilingual,

00:01:58.685 --> 00:02:02.021 align:start size:94% position:6%
whether they could
speak English or not.

00:02:02.021 --> 00:02:04.224 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:04.224 --> 00:02:10.330 align:start size:94% position:6%
Just on the chance that
somebody only spoke Romanian

00:02:10.330 --> 00:02:12.432 line:92%
and needed a chicken biscuit.

00:02:12.432 --> 00:02:15.368 align:start size:94% position:6%
So they would be
calling back orders to me,

00:02:15.368 --> 00:02:17.804 size:81% position:41%
I wouldn't understand
what they were saying.

00:02:17.804 --> 00:02:18.404 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
They'd be like,

00:02:18.404 --> 00:02:21.174 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Yes, I need a bacon, egg,
and cheese on biscuit."

00:02:21.174 --> 00:02:21.841 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
And I'd be like,

00:02:21.841 --> 00:02:24.544
"I'ma just give you the sandwich
I was working on

00:02:24.544 --> 00:02:27.380 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
and hopefully..."

00:02:27.380 --> 00:02:29.983 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:29.983 --> 00:02:33.219 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Hopefully their flight
leaves soon."

00:02:33.219 --> 00:02:33.820 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:33.820 --> 00:02:37.223
I can't get in trouble if they
complain in another country.

00:02:37.223 --> 00:02:39.392 size:84% position:42% line:92%
I can't get in trouble.

00:02:39.392 --> 00:02:42.762 line:92%
They complain in the sky.

00:02:42.762 --> 00:02:44.631 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I'm pro bullying.

00:02:44.631 --> 00:02:46.733 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:46.733 --> 00:02:47.400 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I went through it.

00:02:47.400 --> 00:02:50.203 align:start size:94% position:6%
I feel like other people
should have to go through it.

00:02:50.203 --> 00:02:51.504 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:51.504 --> 00:02:54.374 align:start size:94% position:6%
I didn't just get bullied
at school.

00:02:54.374 --> 00:02:56.075 size:88% position:44% line:92%
I got bullied at church.

00:02:56.075 --> 00:02:57.377 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Audience aws ]

00:02:57.377 --> 00:02:58.878 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Family outings.

00:02:58.878 --> 00:03:02.549
I'm the only person I know
that got bullied in college.

00:03:02.549 --> 00:03:06.319 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was well-rounded,
but well bullied.

00:03:06.319 --> 00:03:07.320 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:07.320 --> 00:03:09.255 align:start size:94% position:6%
I remember one time
when I was a kid,

00:03:09.255 --> 00:03:12.258 align:start size:94% position:6%
these kids took my birthday
cards out of my mailbox

00:03:12.258 --> 00:03:16.196
and ripped up the checks
that I got for my birthday

00:03:16.196 --> 00:03:18.798 align:start size:94% position:6%
and put them
in front of my house.

00:03:18.798 --> 00:03:23.236
I remember thinking, "Man,
they remembered my birthday."

00:03:23.236 --> 00:03:25.405 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:25.405 --> 00:03:29.409 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Applause ]

00:03:29.409 --> 00:03:33.513 align:start size:94% position:6%
I feel like a way of
adult bullying

00:03:33.513 --> 00:03:36.950 align:start size:94% position:6%
is people keep asking me,
"How old are you?"

00:03:36.950 --> 00:03:40.453 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:40.453 --> 00:03:42.889 size:78% position:39%
Like, I don't have to
answer that question.

00:03:42.889 --> 00:03:46.593 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I'm grown.

00:03:46.593 --> 00:03:48.928 align:start size:94% position:6%
Sometimes people try
to guess my age.

00:03:48.928 --> 00:03:51.331 align:start size:94% position:6%
They always guess an age
that's too young.

00:03:51.331 --> 00:03:53.333 align:start size:94% position:6%
They're always like,
"Are you 12?"

00:03:53.333 --> 00:03:55.401 line:92%
I'm like, "No, I'm not 12.

00:03:55.401 --> 00:03:59.038
You don't know any 12-year-olds
that act like this.

00:03:59.038 --> 00:04:01.641 line:92%
I have too much swag to be 12."

00:04:01.641 --> 00:04:02.809 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:02.809 --> 00:04:06.779 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:08.314 --> 00:04:11.351
Everywhere I go, people want to
talk about politics.

00:04:11.351 --> 00:04:15.655
People in waiting rooms,
people in bars, people in Ubers.

00:04:15.655 --> 00:04:21.594
Like, these people are extras
in the movie that is my life.

00:04:21.594 --> 00:04:26.332 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:26.332 --> 00:04:29.936 align:start size:94% position:6%
But they feel like
they have speaking parts.

00:04:29.936 --> 00:04:31.571 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:31.571 --> 00:04:36.342 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:39.679 --> 00:04:41.914 size:75% position:38%
I don't need to hear
what you got to say.

00:04:41.914 --> 00:04:43.516 line:92%
You're not in the credits.

00:04:43.516 --> 00:04:46.686 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:48.755 --> 00:04:50.590 align:start size:94% position:6%
I feel like
part of the problem is

00:04:50.590 --> 00:04:52.659 align:start size:94% position:6%
we're too focused
on the big issues.

00:04:52.659 --> 00:04:55.995
Maybe we should start with
a small issue we can solve

00:04:55.995 --> 00:04:58.965 align:start size:94% position:6%
and work our way
up to the big issues.

00:04:58.965 --> 00:05:02.669 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:02.669 --> 00:05:04.604 line:92%
Like, here's a small issue.

00:05:04.604 --> 00:05:07.640 align:start size:94% position:6%
Are we chipping,
or are we swiping?

00:05:07.640 --> 00:05:09.509 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:05:09.509 --> 00:05:14.447 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:14.447 --> 00:05:16.849 align:start size:94% position:6%
I feel like we've done
a great job

00:05:16.849 --> 00:05:17.950 line:92%
of distributing the chip card.

00:05:17.950 --> 00:05:23.723 align:start size:94% position:6%
I feel like everybody has
a computer chip on their card.

00:05:23.723 --> 00:05:25.158 line:92%
It's supposed to keep you safe.

00:05:25.158 --> 00:05:29.395
You know, bad guys, they don't
know about computer chips yet.

00:05:29.395 --> 00:05:32.532 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:05:32.532 --> 00:05:34.801 align:start size:94% position:6%
Then you get to the register,
and they're like,

00:05:34.801 --> 00:05:39.238 align:start size:94% position:6%
"I'm sorry, sir,
we're swiping today."

00:05:39.238 --> 00:05:42.775 align:start size:94% position:6%
Then the next time
you try to swipe,

00:05:42.775 --> 00:05:45.244 align:start size:94% position:6%
they're like, "Whoa, whoa,
put the chip in!

00:05:45.244 --> 00:05:49.082
You'll blow this whole place up
if you don't put that chip in!"

00:05:49.082 --> 00:05:50.283 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:50.283 --> 00:05:55.488 align:start size:94% position:6%
"I'ma lose my job
if one more person swipes!"

00:05:55.488 --> 00:05:56.456 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Thank you.

00:05:56.456 --> 00:05:58.725 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:58.725 --> 00:06:02.195 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
♪♪♪♪

00:06:02.195 --> 00:06:06.666 line:92%
-Blowing the whole place up.

00:06:06.666 --> 00:06:10.036 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
